    <span class="tag tag-purple">Speculative Decoding</span>
    <span class="tag tag-cyan">Training Systems</span>
    <span class="tag tag-green">Interactive</span>
  </div>
  <h1>TorchSpec: Training Draft Models by Streaming Hidden States, Not Storing Them</h1>
  <p class="lead">Training an EAGLE-3 draft model for a 1-trillion-parameter target like Kimi K2.5 means moving an enormous river of hidden states — one 128K-token sample alone is 7 GB. The old answers are bad: co-locate training with inference and you're stuck at 4K context on a single node, or dump everything offline and you're staring at 700 TB of disk. TorchSpec is a torch-native framework that <strong>disaggregates</strong> the two and streams hidden states straight from inference engines to training workers over the network — zero disk, independent scaling, 200K-token context.</p>
