<!-- ===================== 07 ===================== -->
<section id="s-ecosystem" data-code="ecosystem">
<div class="section-no">07 — Ecosystem &amp; roadmap</div>
<h2>Where TorchSpec sits next to SpecForge</h2>
<p>Both projects train EAGLE-3 drafts; they answer to different masters. <strong>SpecForge</strong> is the SGLang team's framework — its goal is that whatever you train drops straight into SGLang serving with no porting, and it leans on memory tricks (FlexAttention for the training-time test, an in-place Triton kernel) to fit big targets on a node. <strong>TorchSpec</strong> is torch-native and inference-engine-agnostic; its goal is to remove the data-movement ceiling entirely so you can train at trillion-parameter, long-context scale.</p>

<table class="results-table">
  <thead><tr><th></th><th>SpecForge</th><th>TorchSpec</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>Maintainer</td><td>SGLang / LMSYS</td><td>LightSeek Foundation</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Core idea</td><td>SGLang-native drafter training</td><td>Disaggregated streaming of hidden states</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Training modes</td><td>Online (co-located) + offline dump</td><td>Disaggregated (stream, no disk)</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Algorithms</td><td>EAGLE-3, DFlash, Domino</td><td>EAGLE-3 (DFlash / MTP on roadmap)</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Inference backends</td><td>SGLang</td><td>vLLM (1st), TokenSpeed (wip), SGLang/HF (community)</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Sweet spot</td><td>Fast path to SGLang deployment</td><td>1T-param targets, 200K context</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h3>TorchSpec backend support</h3>
<table class="results-table">
  <thead><tr><th>Backend</th><th>Tier</th><th>Status</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>vLLM</td><td class="best">First-class</td><td>Available</td></tr>
    <tr><td>TokenSpeed</td><td class="best">First-class</td><td>In progress</td></tr>
    <tr><td>SGLang</td><td>Community</td><td>Available (patch)</td></tr>
    <tr><td>HuggingFace Transformers</td><td>Community</td><td>Available</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h3>What ships today</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Released drafts:</strong> EAGLE-3 models for Kimi K2.5 / K2.6 (incl. MLA and EAGLE-3.1 variants), MiniMax-M2.5/M3, and Qwen3 — plus the open 600k-sample training dataset.</li>
  <li><strong>Training features:</strong> FSDP checkpoints, vocabulary pruning, resume vs. continual modes, HF-format conversion, W&amp;B logging, per-rank file logs via <code>TORCHSPEC_LOG_DIR</code>.</li>
  <li><strong>Ready-to-run configs:</strong> single-node 4-GPU up to 5-node H200, including <code>kimi-k25-2node-h200</code> and <code>kimi-k25-3node-h100</code>.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Roadmap</h3>
<ul>
  <li>More targets: MiniMax M2.5, Qwen 3.5, GLM 5</li>
  <li>Packed-sequence training for higher throughput</li>
  <li>Algorithms beyond EAGLE-3: DFlash, MTP</li>
  <li>TensorRT-LLM integration</li>
</ul>

<div class="callout">If you live in SGLang and want a drafter <em>today</em>, SpecForge is the shortest path. If your target is a trillion-parameter MoE and you need real long-context training without a 700 TB filesystem, TorchSpec's disaggregation is the architecture built for that problem.</div>
</section>

<!-- Listen-friendly content (hidden summary played during audio playback) -->
<div class="listen-friendly-content" style="display: none;" aria-hidden="true">
  <div lang="en">
    <h2>Audio Summary: TorchSpec — Disaggregated Speculative Decoding Training</h2>
    <p>Speculative decoding speeds up large language models by pairing them with a small draft model that guesses several tokens ahead, which the big target model then verifies in a single parallel pass. The modern method, EAGLE-3, trains the draft model on the target's internal hidden states. The trouble is scale: for a trillion-parameter target like Kimi K2.5, a single 128,000-token training sample produces about 7 gigabytes of hidden states. A 100,000-sample dataset would be 700 terabytes. So the real problem in draft-model training is not the math — it is moving an enormous volume of activation data.</p>
    <p>Before TorchSpec, there were two options, both bad. Co-located online training puts the target and the trainer on the same GPUs, but the 575-gigabyte target leaves almost no memory for training — about 8 gigabytes per card on an H100 — capping context length near 4,000 tokens and locking you to a single node. Offline training dumps every hidden state to disk and trains separately, which is flexible but means owning hundreds of terabytes of files and a constant input-output bottleneck.</p>
    <p>TorchSpec disaggregates the two. One cluster runs inference engines like vLLM or SGLang and does nothing but generate hidden states; a separate cluster runs FSDP and does nothing but train the draft. Between them, a transfer engine called Mooncake streams the tensors over the network using zero-copy GPU-Direct RDMA, so the data never touches disk. Each side scales independently, the trainer gets the full GPU memory, and context length jumps to 44,000 tokens on H100 or 200,000 on B200. TorchSpec used this to train an EAGLE-3 draft for Kimi K2.5 in 1,500 H200 GPU-hours over 6 billion tokens, improving output throughput by 60 percent at batch size one. Compared to SpecForge — the SGLang team's framework focused on native deployment and memory tricks — TorchSpec is torch-native and engine-agnostic, built for trillion-parameter, long-context training.</p>
  </div>
  <div lang="zh">
    <h2>语音摘要：TorchSpec — 解耦式投机解码训练</h2>
    <p>投机解码通过给大模型配一个小的草稿模型来加速：草稿模型一次猜出若干个未来的 token，再由大的目标模型在一次并行前向中验证。当前主流方法 EAGLE-3 是用目标模型内部的隐藏状态来训练草稿模型。难点在于规模:对于像 Kimi K2.5 这样的万亿参数目标,单个 12.8 万 token 的训练样本就会产生约 7 GB 的隐藏状态,10 万样本的数据集高达 700 TB。所以草稿模型训练真正的瓶颈不是算法,而是搬运海量的激活数据。</p>
    <p>在 TorchSpec 之前有两种方案,都有缺陷。共置在线训练把目标模型和训练器放在同一批 GPU 上,但 575 GB 的目标几乎不留训练显存——在 H100 上每卡仅约 8 GB,上下文长度被压到 4000 token 左右,且只能单节点。离线训练把所有隐藏状态写到磁盘再单独训练,虽然灵活,却要承受数百 TB 的文件和持续的 I/O 瓶颈。</p>
    <p>TorchSpec 把两者解耦。一个集群跑 vLLM 或 SGLang 等推理引擎,只负责生成隐藏状态;另一个集群跑 FSDP,只负责训练草稿模型。中间由名为 Mooncake 的传输引擎通过零拷贝 GPU-Direct RDMA 在网络上直接流式传输张量,数据完全不落盘。两侧独立扩展,训练器拿到完整显存,上下文长度在 H100 上提升到 4.4 万、在 B200 上达到 20 万 token。TorchSpec 以此用 1500 个 H200 GPU 小时、60 亿 token 训出了 Kimi K2.5 的 EAGLE-3 草稿模型,在 batch size 为 1 时吞吐提升 60%。相比 SGLang 团队主打原生部署与显存优化的 SpecForge,TorchSpec 是 torch 原生、引擎无关,专为万亿参数、长上下文训练而生。</p>
  </div>
</div>

</article>

